WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.170
- [Kelly:] I'm just curious
with a voice like yours,

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:06.060
like were people just like, 'oh my God?'

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.340
from childhood with you?

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.360
Like do you remember
the first time you sang?

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.500
- [Ann Wilson:] Well, uh...

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.030
- People were floored.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:15.250
- My family was super musical.

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:17.010
We had all these aunts
and uncles and everything.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.500
We always loved to play,

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.800
like get together and play the ukuleles,

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:22.700
and sing the old songs and stuff.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:26.050
And so it was pretty
easy just to go from that

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.330
to being asked to sing

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:29.990
at one of my parents' cocktail parties.

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:30.823
- It was fluid.

00:00:30.823 --> 00:00:32.248
Yeah, you're really used to it.

00:00:32.248 --> 00:00:33.081
- It wasn't much of a stretch really.

00:00:33.081 --> 00:00:33.914
- Yeah.

00:00:33.914 --> 00:00:34.747
- And as a little kid,

00:00:34.747 --> 00:00:36.130
you know little kids loved to show off

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:37.860
in front of the grownups, you know?

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:38.693
- Yeah. 'Look at me!'

00:00:38.693 --> 00:00:40.620
- Yeah. Well, yeah.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.453
'I'm funny. Right?'

00:00:41.453 --> 00:00:42.413
- Yeah.

00:00:42.413 --> 00:00:44.150
- You know, and so I used to do this,

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:47.540
I think from early age like six to eight,

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.630
I was doing this rendition
of the Hawaiian Wedding Song

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:52.320
as Ethel Merman.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.990
So it was like a child, you know?

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:58.360
So I think that's where
I got the sort of feeling

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:01.070
that singing and acting go together.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:03.100
- Yeah. Oh, I do agree with that.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.840
Like while I'm singing,
but are you like thi-

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:07.130
Because I hate acting, but I love-

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:09.360
I feel like I do it on stage
because you jump into character

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:10.810
of wherever you were
when you wrote the song.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:11.643
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:11.643 --> 00:01:14.972
That ever hard for you
depending upon this song?

00:01:14.972 --> 00:01:17.240
- For me, it's not the
songs that are too intense.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:19.410
It's the ones that I've grown out of.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:20.243
- Ah.

00:01:20.243 --> 00:01:21.076
- Like, you know

00:01:21.076 --> 00:01:23.950
I don't want to say anything
about too specific songs, but-

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.630
- You don't want to like poo
poo on the songs, but yeah.

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:27.200
- But a song like magic man, you know.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.033
- Yeah.

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:31.300
- Was written way back when I
was in my super early twenties

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:32.790
and with my first love. and-

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:35.620
- Don't you bash Magic
Man right now, ma'am.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:36.453
- That's what I meant.

00:01:36.453 --> 00:01:37.753
- I will actually tackle you.

